    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0608" n="492" xml:id="pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11756.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-28T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I beg to quote the following communication just received from British Admiral
                    Cradock: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>If you will permit me, in consequence of difficulty you may perhaps have
                            in communicating with Brazilian Minister in Mexico, I propose pending
                            contrary instructions to contrive to do all in my power as heretofore in
                            the interests of the United States of America, observing at the same
                            time strict neutrality. Should you desire to do so, will you most kindly
                            inform Washington.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christopher Cradock</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rear Admiral, British Navy</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
